  "ai_language_tip": "Speak clear, polite Standard Modern Greek (el); Cypriots understand Standard Greek though they speak Cypriot Greek; English is widely spoken in Cyprus (switch if staff offers) and in Greek tourist areas, much less at Greek state services and village shops.",
  "english_ok": "sometimes — Very common in Cyprus and in Greek islands/Athens centre hotels and restaurants; limited at Greek public services, village tavernas, garages and older shopkeepers.",
  "politeness": "Use plural 'εσείς' with strangers; open with 'Καλημέρα' (until early afternoon) or 'Καλησπέρα' + who you call for ('τηλεφωνώ εκ μέρους του/της...'); close with 'Ευχαριστώ πολύ, καλή συνέχεια'. Tone is warm and conversational.",
  "name_tip": "Surname first ('στο όνομα Παπαδόπουλος'); Greek surnames change by gender (Παπαδόπουλος / Παπαδοπούλου), give the exact form; spell foreign names in Latin letters and expect Greek transliteration.",
  "phone_tip": "Greece: 10 digits, no trunk 0 — mobile 69x xxx xxxx, Athens landline 21x xxx xxxx; Cyprus: 8 digits — mobile 9x xxx xxx, landline 2x xxx xxx; Viber/WhatsApp often on the same mobile.",
  "time_tip": "24-hour clock in writing; spoken 'επτάμισι' = 7:30 and 'οχτώ παρά τέταρτο' = 7:45 (eight minus a quarter); 'απόγευμα' is afternoon roughly 17:00–20:00, 'βράδυ' after that; dinner bookings at 21:00–22:00 are normal; read back in 24h.",
  "number_tip": "Greek phone numbers are often read in groups (210 / 12 34 567); 'τρία' vs 'τρεις' and 'τέσσερα' vs 'τέσσερις' change with gender ('τρεις άνθρωποι'); in Cyprus English digits are common.",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid the afternoon quiet hours (about 15:00–17:30, mesimeri), restaurant peaks around 14:00 and 21:00–22:30, calls after 21:00, and Sundays for non-hospitality; in August many small businesses close for holidays (around 15 August).",
  "closed_days": "Traditional retail hours: Mon/Wed/Sat close mid-afternoon, Tue/Thu/Fri reopen in the evening after a long break (gr); most shops closed Sunday except tourist areas; Orthodox Easter (moves yearly), 15 August, 25 March and 28 October shut most offices (cy has its own national days such as 1 April and 1 October).",
  "booking_channels": "Doctoranytime for private doctors (gr); the national phone booking line / finddoctors.gov.gr / MyHealth for public hospital clinics (gr); GESY portal with personal doctor referral (cy); efood and Wolt for delivery (gr), Foody, Wolt and Bolt Food (cy); phone and Instagram/Viber common for tavernas, salons and small hotels.",
  "voice_menu": "Telecoms (Cosmote, Vodafone, Nova; Cyta, Epic, PrimeTel in cy), banks, utilities and public services use keypad IVR; tavernas and small shops answer directly on landline or mobile.",
  "callback_habits": "Small businesses call back from a mobile or reply on Viber/WhatsApp; public hospital outpatient booking is by the national phone line or online (gr); OKYPY online requests are confirmed by a phone call within about 48 hours (cy).",
